-- A transmissibility multiplier sealing two blocks in a compositional run.  A
-- column of 20 cells is split into two blocks of ten, each its own
-- equilibration region: the upper block is equilibrated at 250 bar and the
-- lower at 155 bar, each with a water zone at its base.  The permeability is
-- uniform; MULTZ = 0 on layer 10 removes the transmissibility between layers
-- 10 and 11 and nothing else.
--
-- No fluid crosses the barrier, so the pressure difference of about 98 bar
-- between layers 10 and 11 persists and both blocks stay at rest.  Without the
-- multiplier the two blocks equalise within the first report step.

------------------------------------------------------------------------
RUNSPEC
------------------------------------------------------------------------
TITLE
   A MULTZ BARRIER BETWEEN TWO COMPOSITIONAL BLOCKS

METRIC

TABDIMS
/
OIL
GAS
WATER
DIMENS
1 1 20 /

COMPS
3 /

FULLIMP /

START
  1 'JAN' 2016  /

REGDIMS
1 1 0 0 /

EQLDIMS
2 200 /

UNIFIN
UNIFOUT

------------------------------------------------------------------------
GRID
------------------------------------------------------------------------
INIT

GRIDFILE
0 1 /

DX
20*5 /
DY
20*100 /
DZ
20*5 /
TOPS
1*2000.0 /
PORO
20*0.3 /
PERMX
20*2000 /
PERMY
20*2000 /
PERMZ
20*2000 /

-- Seal the face between layers 10 and 11.
MULTZ
9*1 0 10*1 /

------------------------------------------------------------------------
PROPS
------------------------------------------------------------------------
CNAMES
CO2
METHANE
DECANE
/

EOS
PR /

BIC
0
0
0
/

ACF
0.22394 0.01142 0.4884
/

PCRIT
73.773
45.992
21.03
/

TCRIT
304.128
190.564
617.7
/

MW
44.00
16.04
142.28
/

VCRIT
0.09412
0.09863
0.60980
/

SGFN
0.0 0.00 0.0
0.1 0.00 0.0
0.2 0.05 0.0
0.4 0.10 0.0
0.6 0.40 0.0
0.8 0.60 0.0
0.99 0.70 0.0
/

SWFN
0.01 0.0  0.0
0.20 0.00 0.0
0.40 0.01 0.0
0.60 0.20 0.0
0.80 0.80 0.0
1.00 1.00 0.0
/

SOF3
0.0 0.00 0.0
0.1 0.00 0.0
0.2 0.05 0.05
0.4 0.10 0.10
0.6 0.40 0.40
0.8 0.60 0.60
0.99 0.70 0.70
/

STCOND
15.0 1.0 /

ROCK
    68.9476  0.0 /

PVTW
    75.0  1.03  4.0E-5  0.3  0.0 /

DENSITY
    800.0  1000.0  1.0 /

-- One table per equilibration region.
ZMFVD
 2000   0 0.7 0.3
 2100   0 0.3 0.7  /
 2000   0 0.7 0.3
 2100   0 0.3 0.7  /

RTEMP
100
/

------------------------------------------------------------------------
REGIONS
------------------------------------------------------------------------
EQLNUM
10*1 10*2
/

------------------------------------------------------------------------
SOLUTION
------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- The water-oil contact of each block lies three layers above its base.
EQUIL
   2010  250  2035  0  2000  0  /
   2060  155  2085  0  2050  0  /

------------------------------------------------------------------------
SUMMARY
------------------------------------------------------------------------
ALL

-- Block values at the top and the base of each block; layers 10 and 11 face
-- each other across the barrier.
BPR
1 1 1 /
1 1 10 /
1 1 11 /
1 1 20 /
/

BGSAT
1 1 1 /
1 1 10 /
1 1 11 /
1 1 20 /
/

BOSAT
1 1 1 /
1 1 10 /
1 1 11 /
1 1 20 /
/

BWSAT
1 1 1 /
1 1 10 /
1 1 11 /
1 1 20 /
/

------------------------------------------------------------------------
SCHEDULE
------------------------------------------------------------------------
RPTRST
BASIC=1
PRESSURE
SGAS
SOIL
SWAT
XMF
YMF
ZMF
DENO
DENG
DENW
/

TSTEP
0.01 0.02 0.1 0.2 1.0 5.0
/
END
